meta {
  name: Patch Pipeline
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datasets/:dataSetId/pipelines/:id
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  ~confirmDataLoss: true
}

params:path {
  dataSetId: {{dataSetId}}
  id: {{pipelineId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "description": "Patched pipeline description"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.body && res.body.id) {
    bru.setVar('pipelineId', res.body.id);
  }
}

tests {
  test("Status code is 200", function() {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  **Precondition:** `dataSetId` and `pipelineId` are set.

  **Expected Response:** 200 OK, body reflects updated `description`; other fields unchanged.

  **Removed DataSinks:** A DataSink that loses its last Pipeline because `dataSinkIds` no longer lists it becomes inactive, with the same effects and the same `confirmDataLoss` rule as `delete-pipeline`. The backend calculates the effects on the state after the request, so an API stays when the request replaces its DataSink with a new one of the same kind. When the request removes stored data and `confirmDataLoss` is not `true`, the backend answers `409` `REMOVAL_NOT_CONFIRMED` with the `removal` list of `delete-pipeline` and changes nothing. The Pipeline of this collection links no DataSink at this point, so the request removes none.

  **System Impact:**

  | Layer | Effect |
  |---|---|
  | Backend | Pipeline `description` updated; other fields unchanged |
  | Config Adapter | -- |
  | External System | -- |
}
